## Why Chunking Matters in the data procesing pipelines

• Better retrieval precision: Focused chunks match specific queries more accurately than bloated or mixed-topic passages.
• Preserved context: Respecting natural boundaries and using overlap keeps complete ideas and surrounding context intact.
• Lower cost and latency: Sending only the most relevant chunks reduces compute overhead, token usage, and response time.
• Fewer hallucinations: Grounding LLMs in clean, relevant segments improves answer accuracy.

## Common Chunking Approaches

• Fixed-size and recursive chunking: Splits text by token/character counts or fallback separators (such as paragraphs and sentences) with optional overlap.
• Semantic chunking: Groups sentences by meaning or embedding similarity rather than arbitrary length.
• Structure-aware and parent-child chunking: Uses headings, sections, or hierarchical pairs to keep structure while balancing retrieval precision and full context.

